      "association_protocol": "The target is whole-community versus whole-environment distance-pattern association on all24matched sample IDs. For cover geometry,normalize each complete44-species estimated-cover row by its own positive row total,then square-root its components;use Euclidean distances. This is a Hellinger representation of relative cover,not a count-of-individuals sample. For environment geometry,use all14listed variables,each centered and divided by its population standard deviation over the same24sites,then Euclidean distances. Environmental variables include bare-soil cover and humus depth;do not relabel all14as chemical concentrations. Canonical row order is sample_id interpreted as ascending integer.",
      "randomization_protocol": "The explicitly requested numerical sensitivity uses9999 independent unrestricted label permutations of the community matrix,seed2026,numpy.default_rng PCG64,greater-tail,plus-one count correction and the documented numerical tie rule. Pairwise distances are not independent randomization units. This is not a validated inferential null for the original spatial/grazing design.",
